WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.520 line:87%
My name is Mina Jaf.
I'm 27 years old and from Kurdistan.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.280 line:87%
Prior to my birth, my mother and I lived
in the Kurdish town Halabja.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.600 line:87%
Halabja was the Kurdish town
gassed by Saddam Hussein in 98.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.760 line:87%
We fled to Denmark,
where I grew up.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.280 line:87%
When I was younger,
my biggest frustration was

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.440 line:94%
how to be a good citizen in society.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:37.200 line:87%
One thing led to another in my quest
to work for the local community.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.760 line:94%
I ended up working with refugees.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.840 line:87%
We submitted a request to get a
volunteer from Erasmus+, EVS,

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.880 line:94%
European Voluntary Services, that is.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.080 line:1%
We were really impressed
when we saw Mina’s application.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.480 line:1%
What a great profile!
She could be really helpful.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:06.440 line:87%
She comes from a refugee background
herself, so she is perfect for the job.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.440 line:87%
She knows very well what refugees
go through on their way to Europe.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.200 line:94%
The refugees are leaving their homes

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.520 line:87%
families, roots,
memories and childhood behind.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.680 line:87%
They're fleeing because of war
and terrible surroundings.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.080 line:94%
They risk their lives when they flee.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.480 line:87%
It takes them
many millions of steps to get here.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.840 line:94%
They have no food, money or clothes.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:44.120 line:87%
Mina deals with the daily planning
and manages a team of 20 people

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.440 line:94%
who take care of the asylum seekers.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:52.600 line:87%
Some of them sleep rough. We
monitor the situation on the streets.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.720 line:87%
Mina does the planning of volunteer
teams for the morning and evening.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.400 line:87%
I'm learning a lot
working in this EVS project.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:06.000 line:87%
It gives me the chance
to develop a lot of personal skills

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.760 line:94%
such as languages, development

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.040 line:87%
management,
leadership and coordination.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.000 line:87%
Our experience with Mina and EVS
has been so positive

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.280 line:87%
that we submitted
a request for a second volunteer.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.840 line:87%
Working together with EVS
has been very straightforward,

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.520 line:87%
compared to other
project applications,

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.840 line:87%
in terms of administration,
content and finances.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.920 line:87%
It is so useful. Working
with volunteers is very important.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.320 line:87%
It gives people the chance to help
asylum seekers and refugees.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.680 line:94%
And it makes our team stronger.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.440 line:87%
When I fled to Denmark, I not only
lost my home, friends and family.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:59.280 line:87%
I also lost the little moments
of picking flowers in the garden

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:04.080 line:87%
and going to the bakery
to get bread in the morning.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.560 line:87%
Always having hope
is the most important thing for me.

